! **The noncollinear GGA branch, with a derivative** -- `h4-noncolin-force.in`
! run with PBE instead of LDA.
!
! The gradient correction of a *vector* magnetization is the one part of the
! noncollinear stack that had no measured number of any kind. Its guard was
! measured (a bare `|m|` differentiated through its own nodes gave nan on 243
! grid components, and `safe_modulus` made them finite) but whether the branch is
! *right* was never checked against anything: every committed PBE reference here
! is collinear or nonmagnetic, and every noncollinear reference is LDA. This file
! is the cell that crosses the two, and its force is what makes the check a
! derivative rather than an energy -- the energy can be right while its
! derivative is wrong, which is the trap this project has paid for more than
! once.
!
! `input_dft` overrides the header rather than swapping the dataset, and that is
! deliberate: `H.pz-vbc.UPF` is an LDA pseudopotential and using it under PBE is
! not a physically converged calculation, but it is the *same* inconsistency on
! both sides of the comparison and it isolates the functional. A PBE hydrogen
! dataset would change the projectors as well as the functional and the
! comparison would no longer say which of the two moved. QE warns about the
! mismatch and runs.
!
! Everything else is `h4-noncolin-force.in` unchanged: four moments 90 degrees
! apart in the xy plane, the second atom pushed along z so every atom has a
! force, norm-conserving, `nosym`, one shifted k-point.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
    tprnfor = .true.
    tstress = .true.
    verbosity = 'high'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 6, celldm(1) = 12.0, celldm(3) = 1.66666666666667,
    nat = 4, ntyp = 4,
    ecutwfc = 25.0,
    occupations = 'smearing', smearing = 'gaussian', degauss = 0.10
    noncolin = .true.
    input_dft = 'PBE'
    nosym = .true.
    starting_magnetization(1) = 0.6, angle1(1) = 90.0, angle2(1) =   0.0
    starting_magnetization(2) = 0.6, angle1(2) = 90.0, angle2(2) =  90.0
    starting_magnetization(3) = 0.6, angle1(3) = 90.0, angle2(3) = 180.0
    starting_magnetization(4) = 0.6, angle1(4) = 90.0, angle2(4) = 270.0
    nbnd = 24
 /
 &electrons
    mixing_beta = 0.1
    electron_maxstep = 300
    conv_thr = 1.0d-11
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 H1  1.008  H.pz-vbc.UPF
 H2  1.008  H.pz-vbc.UPF
 H3  1.008  H.pz-vbc.UPF
 H4  1.008  H.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (crystal)
 H1 0.0 0.0 0.00
 H2 0.0 0.0 0.27
 H3 0.0 0.0 0.50
 H4 0.0 0.0 0.75
K_POINTS {automatic}
 1 1 1 0 0 1
